# Complexity Analysis

### Time Complexity

Each binary search step eliminates approximately half of the array.

```text
O(log N)
```

### Space Complexity

Only a few variables are used:

```text
O(1)
```

---

# Important Binary Search Pattern

This problem uses a different type of binary search.

We are **not searching for a specific value**.

Instead, we are using the **direction of the array** to decide which half contains a peak.

```text
nums[mid] < nums[mid + 1]
        ↓
   Go Right

nums[mid] > nums[mid + 1]
        ↓
    Go Left
```

---

# Key Takeaway

Whenever a problem asks you to find a **peak** and requires `O(log N)`, think:

```text
Binary Search
     ↓
Compare nums[mid] and nums[mid + 1]
     ↓
If increasing → move right
If decreasing → move left
     ↓
left == right
     ↓
Peak Element
```

The final index is guaranteed to be a valid peak because the array has no equal adjacent elements.
